// migration.proto — DashCenter northbound ENI live-migration API.
//
// This service is the operator-facing surface of the 10-phase ENI live
// migration state machine described in
// specs/ENI-MIGRATION/dashcenter_eni_live_migration_design_spec.md.
//
// Why a separate service?
// -----------------------
// ENI migration crosses ControlPlane (write), OperationsService (drain),
// HaService (role flip), and ObservabilityService (drift) concerns. A
// dedicated service keeps the rich phase-aware control surface from
// polluting the simpler CRUD shape of ControlPlane, and makes it easy to
// gate migration features behind a capability or feature-flag.
//
// State machine
// -------------
// Phases follow MigrationPhase below. Transitions are linear (each phase
// must be the immediate successor of the previous one) EXCEPT for terminal
// rollback transitions:
//
//   ADMISSION -> SNAPSHOT -> PREPARE -> SYNC -> READY -> CUTOVER
//        -> DRAIN -> COMMIT -> FINALIZE -> [COMPLETED]
//
//   any non-terminal phase -> ROLLBACK -> [ABORTED]
//
// Optimistic concurrency
// ----------------------
// Each AdvanceMigrationPhase call carries the expected_generation it
// observed. dashd returns FAILED_PRECONDITION if any other actor has
// progressed the session in the meantime. This makes the API safe to
// drive from multiple operator tools concurrently.
//
// Bundle export/import
// --------------------
// ExportMigrationBundle/ImportMigrationBundle stream a self-contained
// MigrationBundle (declared state slice + observed flows + cutover plan).
// Used for cold-migration (source DPU offline) and for debugging stuck
// migrations offline.

